+Conventions (follow exactly):
+- solution.py must define `class Solution` with the method `{method}` (keep the signature from the statement's starter code). Include `from typing import *` and any other imports at the top.
+- Tests call `Solution().{method}(*args)` directly with the positional args; samples are in samples/*.json as {{"args": [...], "expected": ...}}.
+- Write brute.py defining `class Solution` with the same method `{method}` (a plain brute force written from the statement).
+- Write gen.py with `gen(rng, size)` returning a TUPLE of positional args, e.g. `([3, 1, 2],)`, and optionally `enumerate_all()` yielding such tuples. Use `rng` (a random.Random) for randomness; include degenerate cases (minimum size, equal values, extremes).
